<section class="page-hero">
  <div id="ambient-canvas" class="ambient-canvas"></div>
  <div class="container page-hero-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">Free Tool</span>
    <h1>Free Readability &amp; Content Score Checker</h1>
    <p>This <strong>free readability checker</strong> scores your content's reading ease, word and sentence counts, keyword density, and passive-voice usage instantly. No signup, nothing leaves your browser.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container contact-grid llms-tool-grid">
    <div>
      <form class="contact-form llms-form" id="rd-form" onsubmit="return false;" aria-label="Readability checker form">
        <div>
          <label for="rd-content">Paste your content</label>
          <textarea id="rd-content" style="min-height: 260px;" placeholder="Paste a paragraph, blog post, or any text you want scored for readability."></textarea>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="rd-keyword">Target keyword (optional)</label>
          <input type="text" id="rd-keyword" placeholder="roof repair cost">
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="contact-info-card llms-preview-card">
      <div class="llms-preview-head">
        <strong>Content score</strong>
        <span id="rd-status" class="llms-status">Paste content to analyze</span>
      </div>
      <div id="rd-results" class="rd-results">
        <div class="rd-score-row">
          <div class="rd-score-circle" id="rd-score-circle">
            <span id="rd-score-num">–</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div id="rd-score-label" class="rd-score-label">No content yet</div>
            <div id="rd-score-sub" class="llms-hint" style="margin:0;">Paste content on the left to see your score</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rd-stats-grid">
          <div class="rd-stat"><span id="rd-words">0</span><label>Words</label></div>
          <div class="rd-stat"><span id="rd-sentences">0</span><label>Sentences</label></div>
          <div class="rd-stat"><span id="rd-avg-words">0</span><label>Words / sentence</label></div>
          <div class="rd-stat"><span id="rd-reading-time">0 min</span><label>Reading time</label></div>
          <div class="rd-stat"><span id="rd-density">–</span><label>Keyword density</label></div>
          <div class="rd-stat"><span id="rd-passive">0</span><label>Possible passive sentences</label></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container llms-explainer">

    <h2>What Is a Readability Score?</h2>
    <p>A readability score estimates how easy a piece of text is to read, based on measurable factors like sentence length and word complexity. This tool uses the <strong>Flesch Reading Ease</strong> formula, one of the most widely used readability metrics, scored from 0 (very difficult, academic/legal text) to 100 (very easy, plain conversational text).</p>

    <h2>How to Read Your Score</h2>
    <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
      <table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:16px 0; font-size:0.95rem;">
        <thead>
          <tr style="border-bottom:2px solid currentColor;">
            <th style="text-align:left; padding:10px 8px;">Score</th>
            <th style="text-align:left; padding:10px 8px;">Reading level</th>
            <th style="text-align:left; padding:10px 8px;">Typical audience</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.3);"><td style="padding:10px 8px;">90&#8211;100</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">Very easy</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">11-year-old student</td></tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.3);"><td style="padding:10px 8px;">60&#8211;70</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">Plain English</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">13&#8211;15-year-old student, general public</td></tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom:1px solid rgba(128,128,128,0.3);"><td style="padding:10px 8px;">30&#8211;50</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">Fairly difficult</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">College-level reader</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="padding:10px 8px;">0&#8211;30</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">Very difficult</td><td style="padding:10px 8px;">College graduate, specialist reader</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>Most blog content aims for the 60&#8211;70 range — easy enough to skim on a phone, without sounding dumbed down. See our guide to <a href="/blog/seo-content-writing-guide-2026">SEO content writing</a> for how readability fits into a broader content strategy.</p>

    <h2>Why Readability Affects SEO</h2>
    <p>Readability isn't a direct Google ranking factor, but it drives the metrics that are: time on page, scroll depth, and whether a reader finishes the article instead of bouncing back to the search results. Content that's needlessly dense for its topic loses readers before they reach the answer they came for &#8212; and a high bounce-back rate is a signal search engines do pick up on over time.</p>

    <h2>What This Tool Checks</h2>
    <ul class="service-points">
      <li><strong>Flesch Reading Ease score</strong> — based on average sentence length and syllables per word</li>
      <li><strong>Word and sentence counts</strong> — plus average words per sentence, a quick signal for overly long, run-on writing</li>
      <li><strong>Estimated reading time</strong> — based on a 200 words-per-minute average adult reading speed</li>
      <li><strong>Keyword density</strong> — how often your target keyword appears relative to total word count, if you provide one</li>
      <li><strong>Possible passive-voice sentences</strong> — flagged using common passive-construction patterns (a heuristic, not a grammar-perfect check)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to Improve a Low Readability Score</h2>
    <ul class="service-points">
      <li>Break long sentences into two shorter ones wherever a natural pause exists</li>
      <li>Replace multi-syllable words with simpler alternatives where meaning doesn't suffer</li>
      <li>Cut filler phrases that add length without adding information</li>
      <li>Read a paragraph out loud — if you run out of breath before the period, the sentence is too long</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Free Readability Checker FAQs</h2>
    <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top: 22px;">
      <details>
        <summary>What is a good Flesch Reading Ease score for a blog post?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Most successful blog content scores between 60 and 70 — easy enough for a broad general audience without feeling oversimplified. Technical or academic content can reasonably score lower.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is a lower readability score always bad?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No. Legal, medical, and academic writing often needs precision that naturally lowers the score. Match the score to your actual audience and subject matter rather than chasing 100 for its own sake.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How accurate is the passive-voice detection?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>It's a pattern-matching heuristic (common "to be" + past-participle constructions), not a full grammatical parse, so treat flagged sentences as worth a second look rather than a definitive verdict.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does keyword density affect my search ranking?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>Not as a direct ranking formula — modern search engines use semantic understanding, not keyword counting. Density here is a sanity check against accidental keyword stuffing, not a target to hit.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does this tool store or send my content anywhere?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No. Everything is calculated in your browser with JavaScript — nothing is uploaded, logged, or stored on any server, including ours.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-band" style="margin-top: 44px;">
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-1"></span>
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-2"></span>
      <h2>Want content written to actually rank?</h2>
      <p>Contomatix writes and optimizes content for both readers and search engines.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
        <a href="https://wa.me/<%= site.whatsappNumber %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-glass">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

